      "text": "Given that \\( n \\) leaves a remainder of 1 when divided by 6, we can express \\( n \\) in the form:\n\\[ n = 6k + 1 \\]\nfor some integer \\( k \\).\n\nWe need to find the remainder when \\( n + 2010 \\) is divided by 6. First, we substitute the expression for \\( n \\) into \\( n + 2010 \\):\n\\[ n + 2010 = (6k + 1) + 2010 = 6k + 2011. \\]\n\nNext, we need to find the remainder when \\( 6k + 2011 \\) is divided by 6. Since \\( 6k \\) is a multiple of 6, it leaves a remainder of 0 when divided by 6. Therefore, we only need to consider the remainder when 2011 is divided by 6. We perform the division:\n\\[ 2011 \\div 6 = 335 \\text{ remainder } 1, \\]\nwhich means\n\\[ 2011 = 6 \\cdot 335 + 1. \\]\nThus, the remainder when 2011 is divided by 6 is 1. Therefore,\n\\[ 6k + 2011 \\equiv 0 + 1 \\equiv 1 \\pmod{6}. \\]\n\nSo, the remainder when \\( n + 2010 \\) is divided by 6 is \\(\\boxed{1}\\).",
